From: pixel_aosp_manifest maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] adevtool: keep strict AOSP 17 property ownership

The GrapheneOS-only gos-dhdutil debugging interface lets the core shell domain
set a vendor-owned property. Generated GrapheneOS device support carries a
broad neverallow escape, but this pristine-AOSP workflow deliberately removes
that escape. AOSP 17 correctly rejects the cross-partition property writer.

Retain the confined debug helper and its ability to publish its result, but do
not grant shell the forbidden vendor property write. Do not add shell to the
system_writes_vendor_properties_violators compatibility attribute.
---
 .../common/sepolicy/vendor/gos_dhdutil.te                      | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/config/mk/google_devices/common/sepolicy/vendor/gos_dhdutil.te b/config/mk/google_devices/common/sepolicy/vendor/gos_dhdutil.te
index 021afcf2..82e5940c 100644
--- a/config/mk/google_devices/common/sepolicy/vendor/gos_dhdutil.te
+++ b/config/mk/google_devices/common/sepolicy/vendor/gos_dhdutil.te
@@ -9,5 +9,4 @@ net_domain(gos_dhdutil)
 allow gos_dhdutil self:global_capability_class_set net_admin;
 allowxperm gos_dhdutil self:udp_socket ioctl SIOCDEVPRIVATE;
 set_prop(gos_dhdutil, vendor_gos_dhdutil_prop)
-set_prop(shell, vendor_gos_dhdutil_prop)
 ')
-- 
2.53.0
